<?xml version="1.0" standalone="yes"?>
<PLUGIN name="RTX-3090-Unlock"
        author="nonkronk"
        version="2026.10.31b"
        pluginURL="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/nonkronk/unraid-3090-unlock/main/RTX-3090-Unlock.plg"
        support="https://github.com/nonkronk/unraid-3090-unlock/issues"
        icon="RTX-3090-Unlock.png">
  <CHANGES>
    ###2026.10.31b
    - Rolled back to the 2026.10.28 behavior (reverts 2026.10.31 and 2026.10.31a).

    ###2026.10.28
    - New plugin icon on the Plugins page.

    ###2026.10.25a
    - Never fail at boot on a GPU Unlock boot entry: fall back to normal NVIDIA, keep the plugin installed and show a notification (previously an Unraid upgrade could move the plugin to plugins-error and leave NVIDIA blacklisted).
    - SHA-256 verification for every download, so updates actually refresh the runtime scripts on the flash.
    - Runtime scripts pinned to a commit on main.

    ###2026.10.25
    - Self-contained installation via Plugins / Install Plugin URL.
    - Include one prebuilt module; accept a separately staged module matching the running kernel.
    - New supported setups receive a boot backup and separate fallback entry; legacy setups can be adopted without rewriting boot options.
    - No automatic reboot or live GPU reset.
  </CHANGES>

